  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-04T18:52:49.659Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "{parameter}_Stretch parameter is not relative to your \"Max Stretch\" value. It does not start the {parameter}_Stretch at 0.0 based on your Max Stretch value, 0 rest, 1.0 being stretched to the set max. If I set max stretch to be too small (in my test case even .5 Max Stretch was too small) then {parameter}_Stretch never even hits 1.0.\nThe only tutorial I saw on this topic never mentioned this or noticed it, but in his video his \"Max Stretch= 0.5\" caused {parameter}_Stretch to start at about .4 and not 0, as well. I would like to be able to scrub through animations, 0 frame -> final frame based upon the relative Max Stretch inputted physbone value instead of whatever it's trying to do currently. I believe this to be a bug so I put it here.\n\nI don't want to have to set max stretch to 5 as a workaround as that ruins the expected effect I was trying to do, when the chain is pulled all the way I want to change states as smoothly as possibly and not have to pull the chain off it's links and have it floating to achieve this.",
